{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review appeals process against misdiagnosis & detention under mental health act",
        "additional_details": "Patients can be detained under the Mental Health Act based on diagnoses and evidence they may dispute. Pre-detention records must be considered, inaccurate medical records independently reviewed, and changes made transparently. Patients must be able to challenge diagnoses without their objections being treated as further evidence of illness. The Government should ensure independent legal support, fair review and accountability, alongside action to reduce avoidable deaths and harm.",
        "background": "Review appeals process against misdiagnosis and what we see as unlawful detention under the Mental Health Act. Patients challenging diagnoses should be protected, provided independent legal support and redress. Review targets to reduce avoidable deaths and harm.",
